<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><a href="/songs/the-red-flag">The Red Flag</a><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Maryland, My Maryland</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Florida, My Florida</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Michigan, My Michigan</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Song of Iowa</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Ode to Labrador</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Democrats, Good Democrats</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1884</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody, a campaign song for Grover Cleveland</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Scout Vespers</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Snoopy's Christmas</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1967</span><span class="sg-chain-h">opens with &quot;O Tannenbaum&quot;</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">O Tannenbaum, du trägst ein' grünen Zweig</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">16th century</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the folk song it is based on</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Der Tannenbaum (August Zarnack)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1820</span><span class="sg-chain-h">first verse kept by Anschütz</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Lauriger Horatius</span><span class="sg-chain-h">its melody</span></li></ul></section>
